{"text": "TIM McDONNELL\n\nEnvironmental journalist and multimedia producer\ncovering the intersection of science, conflict, business, and politics.\n\ntim.m.mcdonnell@gmail.com @timmcdonnell www.timmcdonnell.org\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nFREELANCE JOURNALIST Reporting on climate change, human rights, science, business, conflict, and other issues\nJuly 2017-Present for The New York Times, The Washington Post, National Public Radio, Bloomberg Businessweek,\nand other outlets, from Washington, D.C., Nigeria, Ghana, and elsewhere.\n\nEditor: Marc Silver / msilver@npr.org\n\nFULBRIGHT-NATIONAL GEOGRAPHIC. A nine-month project to produce multimedia stories on the impacts of climate change to\nSTORYTELLING FELLOW food security and agriculture in Kenya, Uganda, and Nigeria, for National Geographic\nJuly 2016-July 2017 and other outlets.\nEditor: April Fehling / afehling@gmail.com\nCLIMATE DESK Climate Desk is a collaboration between Mother Jones, The Guardian,\nASSOCIATE PRODUCER/ Huffington Post, Slate, The Atlantic, Wired, Grist, and the Center for Invesitgative\nSTAFF ENVIRONMENT REPORTER Reporting that produces original multimedia journalism on climate change. Regularly pitch,\nMother Jones report, and produce stories on energy, politics, natural disasters, economic development,\nJune 2011-July 2016 and science, including travel across the U.S., Europe, and Africa.\nEditor: Clara Jeffery / 415-321-1720 / cjeffery@motherjones.com\nNEWS EDITOR Report and edit daily campus news; oversee daily print production;\nArizona Daily Wildcat manage a staff of reporters.\nMarch-Dec. 2009 Editor: Alex Dalenberg / 520-261-8269 / alex.dalenberg@gmail.com\nAdditional reference Arran Bardige, business data partner at The Guardian / 857-998-7521 / abardige@gmail.com\nsemen EDUCATION werner\nUNIVERSITY OF ARIZONA Bachelor of Arts in Honors English, with a minor in ecology and\nDecember 2010 evolutionary biology.\nGPA: 3.46\n~n AWARD S rere\nFellow, International Reporting Project Grant to support travel in West Africa to report on climate change and conflict resolution.\n\nat the New America Foundation\nOctober-December 2017\n\nMedia fellow, Vermont Law School Two-week residency studying international trade law as it relates to the environment.\nJune 2015\nGrantee, European Journalism Centre Two-month grant to produce a longform multimedia feature\nSummer 2014 on gold mining boomtowns in Ivory Coast, Tanzania, Zambia, and Mozambique\n\nfor The Economist.\n\nWorkshop fellow, MIT Week-long educational workshop at MIT's Knight Science Journalism program\nDecember 2013 focused on climate science and energy markets.\n\nClimate Media Fellow, Heinrich Boell Foundation \u2014_Two-week reporting trip in Germany to produce a multimedia feature for\nOctober 2013 Mother Jones on how the country\u2019s addiction to coal is undermining its\nclean energy revolution.\n\nFellow, Metcalf Institute Week-long educational workshop at the University of Rhode Island's\nJune 2013 Graduate School of Oceanography focused on climate science.\nsn MULTIMEDIA SKILLS -resrneninnnitinnnnnnennnnnent\n\n@ DSLR PHOTO & VIDEO @ PREMIERE @ PHOTOSHOP @ iLLustRATOR) = @ SOCIAL",
